--TEST--
`Core\Reflect\AttributeInfo::name` returns the full name of the declaration a payload is written under, `Shop\Storable::Index` for an owned one and `Shop\Job` for one at namespace level, however the use writes it — `rule:attributes/a-retrieval-matches-the-declaration-it-names`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-the-places-it-may-be-used
// covers: Core\Reflect\AttributeInfo::name
namespace Shop;

abstract class Storable {
    repeatable attribute Index on class { columns: string }
}

attribute Job on method { queue: string }

// The first use writes the short name, and the second writes `Storable::Index`.
// Both name the same declaration.
#[Index(columns: "email")]
#[Storable::Index(columns: "name")]
class Customer extends Storable {
    #[Job(queue: "mail")]
    public function notify(): int {
        return 1;
    }
}

var $described = Core\Reflect::forObject(new Customer());
foreach ($described->attributes() as Core\Reflect\AttributeInfo $attribute) {
    echo $attribute->name(), " on ", $attribute->target() == "" ? "<class>" : $attribute->target(), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
Shop\Storable::Index on <class>
Shop\Storable::Index on <class>
Shop\Job on notify
